<P STYLE="text-align: right; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>Exhibit
99.1</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><IMG SRC="ex99-1_001.jpg" ALT=""></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>Chijet
Announces Receipt of Nasdaq Notification Regarding Minimum Bid Price Compliance</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: normal">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>New
York, October 20, 2025</B> &mdash; <I>CHIJET MOTOR COMPANY, INC. </I>(NASDAQ: CJET) (&ldquo;Chijet&rdquo; or the &ldquo;Company&rdquo;)
today announced that it received a letter from The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC (&ldquo;Nasdaq&rdquo;), notifying the Company that it is currently
not in compliance with the minimum bid price requirement set forth under Nasdaq Listing Rule 5550(a)(2) because the closing bid price
of the Company&rsquo;s Class A ordinary shares was below $1.00 per share for a period of 30 consecutive business days. This press release
is issued pursuant to Nasdaq Listing Rule 5810(b), which requires prompt disclosure of receipt of a deficiency notification. The notification
has no immediate effect on the listing of the Company&rsquo;s ordinary shares, which will continue to trade uninterrupted on Nasdaq under
the ticker &ldquo;CJET.&rdquo;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Pursuant
to Nasdaq Listing Rule 5810(c)(3)(A), the Company has a compliance period of 180 calendar days, or until April 13, 2026 (the &ldquo;Compliance
Period&rdquo;), to regain compliance with Nasdaq&rsquo;s minimum bid price requirement. If at any time during the Compliance Period,
the closing bid price per share of the Company&rsquo;s Class A ordinary shares is at least $1.00 for a minimum of 10 consecutive business
days, Nasdaq will provide the Company a written confirmation of compliance and the matter will be closed. If the Company does not regain
compliance with the minimum bid price requirement within the Compliance Period, the Company may be eligible for additional time, assume
the absence of other deficiencies.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company intends to monitor the closing bid price of its Class A ordinary shares and will, if appropriate, consider implementing available
options, including, but not limited to, implementing a reverse stock split of its ordinary shares, to regain compliance with the minimum
bid price requirement under the Nasdaq Listing Rules.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>About
Chijet Motor Company, Inc.</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B></B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
primary business of Chijet is the development, manufacture, sales, and service of traditional fuel vehicles and NEVs. State-of-the-art
manufacturing systems and stable supply chain management enable the Company to provide consumers with products of high performance at
reasonable prices. In addition to its large modern vehicle production base in Jilin, China, a factory in Yantai, China will be dedicated
to NEV production upon completion of its construction. Chijet has a management team of industry veterans with decades of experience in
engineering and design, management, financing, industrial production, and financial management. For additional information about Chijet,
please visit <U>www.chijetmotors.com</U>.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>Forward-Looking
Statements</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B></B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">This
press release contains forward-looking statements as defined under Section 27A of the Securities Act of 1933 and Section 21E of the Securities
Exchange Act of 1934, formulated in accordance with the &lsquo;safe harbor&rsquo; provisions of the Private Securities Litigation Reform
Act of 1995. These statements, reflecting the Company&rsquo;s projections about its future financial and operational performance, employ
terms like &lsquo;believes,&rsquo; &lsquo;estimates,&rsquo; &lsquo;anticipates,&rsquo; &lsquo;expects,&rsquo; &lsquo;plans,&rsquo; &lsquo;projects,&rsquo;
&lsquo;intends,&rsquo; &lsquo;potential,&rsquo; &lsquo;target,&rsquo; &lsquo;aim,&rsquo; &lsquo;predict,&rsquo; &lsquo;outlook,&rsquo;
